diff --git a/docs/extending.rst b/docs/extending.rst
index be3a277b..feb9f48b 100644
--- a/docs/extending.rst
+++ b/docs/extending.rst
@@ -247,6 +247,14 @@ It is possible to report errors on fields and subfields using a `dict`.
 
 When multiple schema-leval validator return errors, the error structures are merged together in the :exc:`ValidationError <marshmallow.exceptions.ValidationError>` raised at the end of the validation.
 
+.. note::
+
+    A `dict` passed to :exc:`ValidationError <marshmallow.exceptions.ValidationError>`
+    is merged into the error structure as-is, so its keys need to be ``data_key``\s
+    for fields that define one. To let marshmallow resolve the ``data_key`` for you,
+    pass the field name as the ``field_name`` argument instead, e.g.
+    ``raise ValidationError("field_b must be greater than field_a", "field_b")``.
+
 .. code-block:: python
 
     from marshmallow import Schema, fields, validates_schema, ValidationError
